The '''Ashpit''' is an alternative floor to the {{s|Mines}} and is unlocked by defeating all of the [[boss]]es inside the {{s|Mines}}. The floor can be accessed by using bombs on the Exit Door of the {{s|Caves}}/{{s|Catacombs}}/{{s|Flooded Caves}} I or II, or at the end of {{s|Downpour}}/{{s|Dross}}. Ashpit's theme is centered around a dry, crumbling wasteland, with an abundance of skeleton enemies and brutal-looking foes.

The Ashpit is significantly more difficult than their [[Chapter 2|standard counterparts]], filled with stone and bone-themed [[Monster|enemies]] that boast greater health and aggression. Most obstacles are [[rock]]s or [[Spiked Rock]]s, and {{e|Poop}}s are almost non-existent. [[Tinted Rock]]s have a high chance of spawning {{e|Tinted Rock Spider}}s. Travelling through it is only advised if you have already acquired {{I|Knife Piece 1}} in {{s|Downpour}} and intend to access the {{s|Corpse}}.

After defeating the Mines II's boss, a door leading to the next alternate chapter - {{s|Mausoleum}} - appears. It requires 2 full hearts to open. The damage taken ignores almost every form of damage reduction, including {{I|The Wafer}} and invincibility. Unlike other methods of health donation, red hearts will not be prioritized over more valuable hearts.

